      "text": "446 multiplied by 448.\n\nBut wait, let me verify the calculations step by step to ensure accuracy.\n\nFirst, 446 multiplied by 400. 446 times 4 is 1,784, so adding two zeros gives 178,400. That seems correct.\n\nNext, 446 multiplied by 40. 446 times 4 is 1,784, so adding one zero gives 17,840. That also looks correct.\n\nThen, 446 multiplied by 8. 400 times 8 is 3,200, 40 times 8 is 320, and 6 times 8 is 48. Adding those together: 3,200 + 320 = 3,520, plus 48 is 3,568. That's correct.\n\nNow, adding all three results together:\n\n178,400 (from 400)  \n+ 17,840 (from 40)  \n+ 3,568 (from 8)  \n= ?\n\nLet's add 178,400 and 17,840 first. 178,400 + 17,840 = 196,240.\n\nThen, add 3,568 to 196,240. 196,240 + 3,568 = 199,808.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me check the addition again.\n\n178,400  \n+17,840  \n= 196,240. That's correct.\n\n196,240  \n+3,568  \n= 199,808. Hmm, that seems correct.\n\nBut wait, 446 multiplied by 448. Let me try another method to verify.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the formula for multiplying two numbers close to a base, like 450.\n\n446 is 4 less than 450, and 448 is 2 less than 450.\n\nSo, using the identity (a - b)(a - c) = a\u00b2 - a(b + c) + bc.\n\nHere, a = 450, b = 4, c = 2.\n\nSo, (450 - 4)(450 - 2) = 450\u00b2 - 450(4 + 2) + (4)(2)\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n450\u00b2 = 202,500\n\n450(4 + 2) = 450 * 6 = 2,700\n\n4 * 2 = 8\n\nSo, putting it all together:\n\n202,500 - 2,700 + 8 = 202,500 - 2,700 is 199,800, plus 8 is 199,808.\n\nThat matches the previous result. So, the product is indeed 199,808.\n\nBut wait, let me do it the standard way to double-check.\n\nMultiplying 446 by 448:\n\nFirst, write it as:\n\n```\n    446\n  x448\n  -------\n```\n\nMultiply 446 by 8: 3,568\n\nMultiply 446 by 40 (shift one position to the left): 17,840\n\nMultiply 446 by 400 (shift two positions to the left): 178,400\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n```\n    3,568\n  17,840\n+178,400\n---------\n  199,808\n```\n\nYes, that's correct.\n\nSo, the product of 446 and 448 is 199,808.\n</think>\n\n# Answer:\n\nNow, sum all the step results: 178,400 + 17,840 + 3,568 = 199,808.\n\nSo, the final computed product is **199,808**.",
